  "body": " Putting It All Together   The graph below shows the rate of change of some quantity over an -second interval. It is piecewise linear : each piece is a straight line segment, so every region between the graph and the axis is a rectangle, a triangle, or a trapezoid. (Recall the trapezoid area formula , using the two parallel sides , and the width between them.)   A piecewise linear graph of r(t) versus t from t = 0 to t = 11. It is constant at 3 from t = 0 to t = 2 (a rectangle region), rises linearly from 3 to 5 from t = 2 to t = 6 (a trapezoid region), falls linearly from 5 to 0 from t = 6 to t = 9 (a triangle region), then jumps to a constant -2 from t = 9 to t = 11 (a rectangle region below the axis). Regions above the axis are shaded blue; the region below is shaded red.       Interval : name the shape, and find its signed area.      Interval : name the shape, and find its signed area.      Interval : name the shape, and find its signed area.      Interval : name the shape, and find its signed area. Be careful with the sign.      Add up your four signed areas to find .      Suppose is the rate of change of some quantity whose value at is . Using the idea from this activity find .    "
